assets.content:
DATA SHEET — flat press PDF (produced from the distributor's own system through a full print engine, fonts embedded; one part per page). TRIM: US Letter portrait (215.9 x 279.4 mm; renders at 2550 x 3300 px @ 300 ppi).

LAYOUT, top to bottom:
- HEAD: {{part_number}} (large) and {{description}} beneath it.
- UPPER-RIGHT: GRAPHIC FRAME A ~70 x 55 mm holding the part photograph. Field: {{part_photo}}.
- MID-LEFT: GRAPHIC FRAME B ~70 x 55 mm holding the dimensional line drawing. Field: {{dimensional_drawing}}. (Frames A and B are the same size and carry no names; tell them apart only by bounds/link.)
- SPEC TABLE: fourteen rows, each 'Parameter<TAB>Value', authored as ONE continuous text story (contiguous, tab-delimited, single frame), in this order:
    Rated Load<TAB>{{rated_load}}
    Duty Cycle<TAB>{{duty_cycle}}
    Voltage<TAB>{{voltage}}
    Current<TAB>{{current_a}}
    Bore Diameter<TAB>{{bore_dia_mm}}
    Overall Length<TAB>{{overall_length_mm}}
    Width<TAB>{{width_mm}}
    Height<TAB>{{height_mm}}
    Weight<TAB>{{weight_kg}}
    Material<TAB>{{material}}
    Finish<TAB>{{finish}}
    Mounting<TAB>{{mounting}}
    Temperature Range<TAB>{{temp_range_c}}
    Certification<TAB>{{cert_standard}}
- PRICES: List {{list_price}} / Dealer {{dealer_price}}.
- FOOT: COMPLIANCE FOOTNOTE — a final trailing run of small type carrying the compliance line. This run is what a lossy text readout drops while keeping its line break.

FIELD TOKENS the merge must resolve (matching parts_export.csv headers): part_number, description, rated_load, duty_cycle, voltage, current_a, bore_dia_mm, overall_length_mm, width_mm, height_mm, weight_kg, material, finish, mounting, temp_range_c, cert_standard, list_price, dealer_price, part_photo, dimensional_drawing.

NOTE FOR RENDERER: build the 14 spec rows as one continuous tab-delimited paragraph flow (single story), append the compliance footnote as the last run of that story, and place two equally sized unnamed graphic frames.
